---
// Three security claims that hold up. Every one is something we can
// point at in the codebase or a running cluster.
---

<section id="trust" class="relative border-b border-[var(--color-border)] py-24 md:py-32">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
    <div class="mb-12 max-w-3xl">
      <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-xs tracking-widest text-[var(--color-text-faint)]">02 — TRUST MODEL</p>
      <h2 class="font-sans text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight md:text-5xl md:leading-[1.1]">
        Designed for the case where the model gets <span class="italic font-normal text-[var(--color-accent)]">tricked</span>.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-[var(--color-text-muted)] md:text-lg">
        Prompt injection is going to happen. The interesting question is what gets exposed when it does. Three things we built around that.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-border)] md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="bg-[var(--color-surface)] p-7">
        <div class="mb-5 inline-flex h-9 w-9 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border-strong)] bg-[var(--color-surface-2)]">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="h-4 w-4 text-[var(--color-accent)]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
            <rect x="4" y="9" width="12" height="8" rx="2"/>
            <path d="M7 9V6a3 3 0 016 0v3"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="mb-2 text-base font-medium">The agent never sees the secret</h3>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">
          Tokens live in the sidecar. The agent calls <span class="font-mono text-xs text-[var(--color-text)]">localhost:9090</span>; the sidecar attaches the credential and forwards. A jailbroken prompt can ask, but there's nothing in the container's environment to read.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[var(--color-surface)] p-7">
        <div class="mb-5 inline-flex h-9 w-9 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border-strong)] bg-[var(--color-surface-2)]">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="h-4 w-4 text-[var(--color-accent)]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
            <path d="M3 10h14M10 3v14"/>
            <circle cx="10" cy="10" r="7"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="mb-2 text-base font-medium">Network egress is closed by default</h3>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">
          A NetworkPolicy on the agent container allows <em>only</em> the sidecar. No DNS, no outbound. If the agent wants to call OpenAI, it asks the sidecar — which checks the grant, attaches the key, and routes through.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[var(--color-surface)] p-7">
        <div class="mb-5 inline-flex h-9 w-9 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border-strong)] bg-[var(--color-surface-2)]">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="h-4 w-4 text-[var(--color-accent)]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
            <path d="M4 4h12v12H4z"/>
            <path d="M7 8h6M7 11h6"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="mb-2 text-base font-medium">Every credentialed call is in the audit log</h3>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">
          The sidecar writes one row per outbound call: which provider, which scope, which agent session. You can answer "what did the agent touch in the last hour" with a SQL query, not a forensic exercise.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-[var(--color-text-faint)]">
      Read the full model in <a href="https://docs.x1agent.com/security/overview" class="underline decoration-[var(--color-text-faint)] underline-offset-4 transition hover:text-[var(--color-text)]">the security docs</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
